06436eb966d36b67" "q-42167/selection/ma-v1/f7be60c5b940d1f901d5f73f9e5def26db94145d2d03a7218335a1def81fb1c2/a9c61c6f10b1e577ed71468d22767159a20a9fe7856dd5dabfb69789eba772d1" "q-42167/selection/ma-v1/f7be60c5b940d1f901d5f73f9e5def26db94145d2d03a7218335a1def81fb1c2/2c5660bbbb7cbe9946e069a0adb79c061166392e374c5e44a50eaa6df930f243" "q-42167/selection/ma-v1/f7be60c5b940d1f901d5f73f9e5def26db94145d2d03a7218335a1def81fb1c2/c82b71fc7af4cf63f8e2138a8871603dd49bc817c6c95f12d6fba911a36576b1" "q-42167/selection/ma-v1/f7be60c5b940d1f901d5f73f9e5def26db94145d2d03a7218335a1def81fb1c2/97884c1bb509803cd3b24e0d97b0415247bbc44095276bb813581ae95ef3d8dd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42167"] :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}7x+14y=21 \\\\ 3x+6y=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 14 & 21 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 14 & 21 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{7}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=3 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=3.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=3-2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-2y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-42167/selection/ma-v1/f7be60c5b940d1f901d5f73f9e5def26db94145d2d03a7218335a1def81fb1c2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186106243 :question/answer-fields 17592186103967] {:db/id "q-42157/selection/ma-v1/7a65f0d76bb9cecc6325403959aa9eb34559cb5f0d9defdbfb7f2e7a2ec0dda2/3b484d8cf95464e10b1c5df118c645e25cdf7f84694e502bd509f53a24a234a1" :answer/id #uuid "29a7e29f-8472-5fe6-83f5-32700c825a5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-6y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42157/selection/ma-v1/7a65f0d76bb9cecc6325403959aa9eb34559cb5f0d9defdbfb7f2e7a2ec0dda2/9bd660bb4cc70bb2aab3e077ee36bdfdd7770067c09015aceca6c99f81ef542b" :answer/id #uuid "c3ab6d43-610f-5eaf-8c6b-9914c535b8e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2-6y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42157/selection/ma-v1/7a65f0d76bb9cecc6325403959aa9eb34559cb5f0d9defdbfb7f2e7a2ec0dda2/0462edf60e2905c5db3d6d250ad85791ebc5b7f4e15eb4f61bbf98324616605c" :answer/id #uuid "331a90f1-f18f-5d14-b638-3e2581cd3c79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+6y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42157/selection/ma-v1/7a65f0d76bb9cecc6325403959aa9eb34559cb5f0d9defdbfb7f2e7a2ec0dda2/a50682b856a71c59e2ce2782e208b560f34