end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 24 & -10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 24 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-6y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-2$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-2,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-42157/selection/ma-v1/7a65f0d76bb9cecc6325403959aa9eb34559cb5f0d9defdbfb7f2e7a2ec0dda2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-20965/selection/45f2072fe99cf5b8b711fbab447749db77775c846583d3f244aac2a21d98642c" :answer/id #uuid "479a3a4c-1728-5e02-ac01-af5b5eb5cebf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20965/selection/842fbd156ca8305686f6743a65223e15155ae7331655dc0ca431c9478a06bcc2" :answer/id #uuid "3469bf8f-be2a-5a0b-843e-caff58d9c53f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20965/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" :answer/id #uuid "9a4bb37e-c84f-5cf8-8f18-ead192b61531" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20965/selection/ad5159bff20e89400e8ca546efff79d156a2d1ff8cbb94c62fc22a8979b23417" :answer/id #uuid "0a7e7ca6-a11a-5a5a-9a97-14afb6231ff5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20965/selection/71bba66f601af80429ccf164a86d99649addfac65d7789b91a307959c1dbcb5d" :answer/id #uuid "90ee7008-4964-5790-b922-595a356b798a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20965/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce6c8407-ce56-53c9-85a5-0972633eca9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-20965/selection/71bba66f601af80429ccf164a86d99649addfac65d7789b91a307959c1dbcb5d" :answer-field/choices ["q-20965/selection/45f2072fe99cf5b8b711fbab447749db77775c846583d3f244aac2a21d98642c" "q-20965/selection/842fbd156ca8305686f6743a65223e15155ae7331655dc0ca431c9478a06bcc2" "q-20965/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" "q-20965/selection/ad5159bff20e89400e8ca546efff79d156a2d1ff8cbb94c62fc22a8979b23417" "q-20965/selection/71bba66f601af80429ccf164a86d99649addfac65d7789b91a307959c1dbcb5d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-20965" :question/id #uuid "1766ca49-3fde-5817-b4dd-1d97ee2424fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-20965" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x+15y=10 \\\\ 2x+6y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 15 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & 15 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+3y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2-3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-20965/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-20965"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-20783/selection/6341b5424b8aa2affced2ce02050877702296cbb266453cc4ee5859a7119d576" :answer/id #uuid "ca381ea9-d232-5773-a478-eec91b8a130e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20783/selection/12754b0f1defbb410bfbc9b5024d3fbdff1290e22b89fc04e21cf01e261fbe5c" :answer/id #uuid "87e30c2a-a23b-55f3-9103-81bee68cb05f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2+4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20783/selection/6f56db1fdad44b849d5aef3d2fd1d6e98016695476b51c7b7270920b420d1337" :answer/id #uuid "a4ace51c-09ca-51d8-adb6-d4c91f51954b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20783/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" :answer/id #uuid "fab5295c-9d1d-5b43-ba0b-b67428a02205" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20783/selection/a16d9749ca0fb6cc7b7f63894f4252b36de77f0012e6df2eef95995aef36edba" :answer/id #uuid "10592a2a-f8da-572f-9d3a-cb12ecc1ec93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20783/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f82045be-6d2e-5a1c-aa6a-3dc9ee2ddd48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-20783/selection/a16d9749ca0fb6cc7b7f63894f4252b36de77f0012e6df2eef95995aef36edba" :answer-field/choices ["q-20783/selection/6341b5424b8aa2affced2ce02050877702296cbb266453cc4ee5859a7119d576" "q-20783/selection/12754b0f1defbb410bfbc9b5024d3fbdff1290e22b89fc04e21cf01e261fbe5c" "q-20783/selection/6f56db1fdad44b849d5aef3d2fd1d6e98016695476b51c7b7270920b420d1337" "q-20783/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" "q-20783/selection/a16d9749ca0fb6cc7b7f63894f4252b36de77f0012e6df2eef95995aef36edba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-20783" :question/id #uuid "2063c8fa-7613-58b2-b7f1-084d25bc48c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-20783" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4y=2 \\\\ 2x+8y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+4y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2-4y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-4y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-20783/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-20783"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4699"] :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3y=1 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y = 0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx - 3y = 1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=1+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=1+3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=⟨1+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4700"] :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=4 \\\\ 4x+10y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{5}{2}y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-8$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-8,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
